Sure! Those latitude/longitude numbers point right at **Google’s headquarters** – the “Googleplex” in Mountain View, California.  
Below I’ll show how you’d hit the Google Maps Geocoding API to get the full place details, plus what the response would look like.

---

### 1️⃣ Call the Geocoding API

```http
GET https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/geocode/json?
    latlng=37.4224764%2C-122.0842499&
    key={YOUR_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY}
```

> *Replace `{YOUR_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY}` with your own API key.*

If you’re testing locally, you can paste the URL into a browser after inserting a valid key:

```
https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/geocode/json?latlng=37.4224764,-122.0842499&key=AIzaSyD...your_key...
```

---

### 2️⃣ What You Get Back

A successful query will return something along these lines (truncated for brevity):

```json
{
   "results" : [
      {
         "address_components": [...],
         "formatted_address":"1600 Amphitheatre Pkwy, Mountain View, CA 94043, USA",
         "geometry":{
            "location":{"lat":37.423021,"lng":-122.083739},
            ...
         },
         "place_id":"ChIJj61dQgK6j4ARw5Z8Yf7tXcI",
         "types":["street_address"]
      }
   ],
   "status":"OK"
}
```

*Key fields explained*

| Field | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| `formatted_address` | Human‑readable street address |
| `geometry.location.lat / lng` | Exact coordinates returned by the API (may differ slightly due to rounding) |
| `place_id` | Unique identifier for the place within Google’s database |

---

### 3️⃣ Quick Example Using JavaScript (Node.js)

```js
const axios = require('axios');

async function reverseGeocode(lat, lng, apiKey) {
  const url = `https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/geocode/json`;
  try {
    const {data} = await axios.get(url, {
      params: { latlng: `${lat},${lng}`, key: apiKey }
    });

    if(data.status !== 'OK') throw new Error(`API error: ${data.status}`);

    console.log(JSON.stringify(data.results[0], null, 2));
  } catch(err){
    console.error(err);
  }
}

reverseGeocode(37.4224764, -122.0842499, process.env.GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY);
```

Running that script prints out the same structure shown above—just replace `process.env.GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY` with your key.

---

#### TL;DR

Those coordinates (`37.4224764`, `–122.0842499`) resolve to:
```
1600 Amphitheatre Parkway
Mountain View, CA 94043
USA
```
Use the `/geocode/json?latlng=` endpoint with a valid API key to retrieve all the detailed information programmatically.
